Temporal Blow-up Analysis of a Fourth-Order Nonlocal Parabolic Equation with Neumann Boundary Conditions

This paper investigates the finite-time blow-up phenomenon for a fourth-order nonlocal parabolic equation subject to Neumann boundary conditions.  The governing equation, exhibiting nonlocal coupling, is formulated as:

\begin{equation}
\label{eq:1}
\frac{\partial u}{\partial t} + \frac{\partial^4 u}{\partial x^4} = |u|^{p-1}u - \frac{1}{a} \int_0^a |u|^{p-1}u \, dx,
\end{equation}

with boundary conditions

\begin{equation}
\label{eq:2}
\frac{\partial u}{\partial x}(0) = \frac{\partial u}{\partial x}(a) = \frac{\partial^3 u}{\partial x^3}(0) = \frac{\partial^3 u}{\partial x^3}(a) = 0
\end{equation
